$DATUM Synthesis and purification of 1-phenylbut-3-en-1-ol (4) and
(Z)-tributyl(styryl)stannane (5) by one-pot allylation-hydrostannation: A
5 mL round bottom flask was charged with benzaldehyde (1) (0.2 mL, 2
mmol), allyltributylstannane (2a) (0.62 mL, 2 mmol) in toluene (4 mL) and
cooled to -35°C. BF3·OEt2 (0.26 mL, 2.1 mmol) was added slowly and the
reaction was allowed to run until complete (∼1h and 15 minutes). B(C6F5)3
(205 mg, 20%) was weighed and added under nitrogen. PMHS (0.24 mL, 2
equiv) was added to it followed by phenylacetylene (0.22 mL, 2 mmol) and
the reaction was allowed to run for 3 h. NEt3 (0.39 mL, 2.8 mmol) was
added. The crude was subjected to column chromatography [silica gel;
90/10 hexane/EtOAc, 1% TEA]. Product: 4, Yield: (78%), and Product: 5,
Yield: (781 mg, 99%). BF3·OEt2 (equiv): 1.05, solvent: toluene, temp: 35
°C, B(C6F5)3 (mol %): 20, reductant: B= PMHS (2). Data for 4: 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) = 2.49-2.56 (m, 3H), 4.72-4.76 (m, 1H), 5.14-5.19 (m,
2H), 5.79-5.87 (m, 1H), 7.28-7.33 (m, 1H), 7.38 (d, J = 4.2 Hz, 4H). 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) = 43.7, 73.2, 118.1, 125.8, 127.4, 128.3,
134.5, 143.9. Data for 5: 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) = 0.77-0.99 (m,
15H), 1.23-1.30 (m, 6H), 1.38-1.48 (m, 6H), 6.23 (d, J = 13.7 Hz, 1H),
7.10-7.54 (m, 5H), 7.64 (d, J = 14.0 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
(ppm) = 10.8, 13.6, 27.2, 29.0, 127.1, 127.2, 128.1, 132.8, 141.5, 147.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study (solvent, stoichiometry, temperature, catalyst
loading, reductant)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A One-Pot Allylation-Hydrostannation Sequence with Recycling of the
Intermediate Tin Waste
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ghosh, Banibrata; Amado-Sierra, Maria Del Rosario I.; Holmes, Daniel;
Maleczka, Robert E. Jr.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
