$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical procedure for the allylation of aldehydes promoted by P4a: To a
suspension of P4a (164 mg, 0.6 mmol) in acetonitrile (1.5 mL) were added
successively benzaldehyde (53 mg, 0.5 mmol) and allyltributyltin (198 mg,
0.6 mmol) at room temperature. After stirred for 3 h (TLC showed the
reaction was completed). The suspension was filtered and washed with
CH3CN (3 x 5 mL). The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure to
furnish the pure product, 3a (71mg, 96%). The resulted polymer P5a (320
mg) was stirred in a solution of HCl (2 M, 15 mL) and Et2O (5 mL) at room
temperature for 24 h. Then filtered and washed with Et2O (3 x 15 mL) to
recover P4a. The Et2O layer was dried and concentrated under reduced
pressure to recover Bu3SnCl (180 mg, 92% based on allyltributyltin).
1-Phenyl-3-buten-1-ol (3a)8 1H NMR (300MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.37-7.26(m, 5H),
5.87-5.78(m, 1H), 5.14(t, 2H, J = 9.1, 9.6 Hz), 4.73(t, 1H, J = 5.4, 7.3
Hz), 2.54-2.49(m, 2H), 2.03(s, 1H); IR (KBr, film): υ 3383, 3076, 3030,
2978, 2906, 1642, 1494, 1455, 1435, 1048, 916, 700 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst, last stage for catalyst recovery
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Allylation of Aldehydes and Imines: Promoted by Reusable
Polymer-Supported Sulfonamide of N-Glycine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Gui-Long; Zhao, Gang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(4), 633-636

