$DATUM 110-54-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A THF solution of LDA was prepared by adding n-butyllithium (1.6 M in
hexanes, 8.46 mL, 13.5 mmol) to a solution of diisopropylamine (1.99 mL,
14.2 mmol) in THF (10 mL) at 0 °C. After complete addition, the mixture
was cooled to -78 °C, and then allyl acetate (0.92 mL, 8.55 mL) was
added. The reaction mixture was stirred for 45 min at -78 °C, and
crotonaldehyde (99.9% trans, 500 mg, 7.13 mmol) was added. After 1 h of
stirring at -78 °C, a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (10 mL) was added,
and the mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate (2 x 50 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with water, dried over anhydrous
MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography (20% EtOAc/hexanes) to
afford alcohol. Colorless alcohol, yield 1.04 g (86%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Anionic Polycyclization Entry to Tricycles Related to Quassinoids and
Terpenoids: A Stereocontrolled Total Synthesis of (+)-Cassaine
