$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Alcohol 21a A LDA solution was prepared by adding n-butyllithium (1.6 M
in hexanes, 8.46 mL, 13.5 mmol) to a solution of diisopropylamine (1.99
mL, 14.2 mmol) in THF (10 mL) at 0°C. After complete addition, the
mixture was brought to -78°C and allyl acetate (0.92 mL, 8.55 mL) was
added. The reaction mixture was stirred for 45 min at -78°C and
crotonaldehyde (99.9% trans, 500 mg, 7.13 mmol) was added. After stirring
for 1h at -78°C, an aqueous ammonium chloride saturated solution was
introduced and the mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate. The combined
organic layers were washed with water, dried over anhydrous magnesium
sulfate, filtered and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue
was purified by flash chromatography (20% EtOAc/Hexanes) to afford 1.04 g
(86%) of a colorless. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ (7.26 ppm): 5.98-5.82 (m,
1H), 5.79-5.64 (m, 1H), 5.57-5.41 (m, 1H), 5.34-5.21 (m, 2H), 4.60 (dt,
2H, J = 1.4, 5.7), 4.54-4.42 (m, 1H), 2.81 (d, 1H, J = 4.1), 2.56-2.53
(m, 2H), 1.69-1.66 (m, 3H) 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 171.9,
131.8, 131.7, 127.5, 118.5, 68.8, 65.3, 41.5, 17.6 LRMS: m/z (relative
intensity): 170 (M+, 4), 155 (9), 129 (70), 111 (99), 87 (100) HRMS:
Calculated for C9H14O3: 170.0943 Found: 170.0938 ± 0.0005 IR (neat/ NaCl)
v (cm-1): 3444, 2934, 1739, 1161
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in situ prepared LDA
