$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (E)-1-(4-Methylphenyl)-2-buten-1-ol (±)-2d7.
Method A: Under a nitrogen atmosphere, to a solution of the carbonyl
compound (14 mmol) in THF (70 mL) was dropwise added the corresponding
Grignard or lithium reagents (21 mmol) at -78 °C. The reaction mixture
was allowed to warm to room temperature and stirred until the complete
consumption of the substrate. After quenching with sat. aq. NH4Cl, the
organic materials were extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic extract
was washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and evaporated in vacuo. The
residue was purified by column chromatography (silica gel) to give (±)-1
or (±)-2, using crotonaldehyde (342 mg, 4.9 mmol), p-MeC6H4Li generated
from p-MeC6H4Br (1.00 g, 5.9 mmol) and n-BuLi (1.57 M in hexanes; 3.70
mL, 5.9 mmol), and THF (20 mL). After 3.5 h at room temperature, work-up
and column chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc = 10:1 to 5:1).
(E)-1-(2-Thienyl)-2-buten-1-ol (±)-2h; (930 mg, 85%); colorless oil. 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.28-7.24 (m, 1H), 6.99-6.96 (m, 2H), 5.88-5.74
(m, 2H), 5.39 (t, J= 5.0 Hz, 1H), 2.02 (br s, 1H), 1.76 (d, J= 6.0 Hz,
3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 147.5, 132.6, 128.2, 126.7, 125.0,
123.9, 71.1, 17.6. IR (CHCl3) :ν: 3593 cm-1. Anal. Calcd for C8H10OS: C,
62.30; H, 6.54. Found: C, 61.96; H, 6.71.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Synthesis of Optically Active Allyl Esters via Lipase-Vanadium
Combo Catalysis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Akai, Shuji; Hanada, Ryosuke; Fujiwara, Noboru; Kita, Yasuyuki; Egi,
Masahiro
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(21), 4900-4903

