$DATUM (3R,4S,E)-4-methyl-1-phenylhexa-1,5-dien-3-ol An oven-dried sealed tube
under an atmosphere of N2 was charged with trans-cinnamyl aldehyde 3f
(26.4 mg, 0.20 mmol, 100 mol%), (S)-I (10.3 mg, 0.01 mmol, 5 mol%), K3PO4
(21.5 mg, 0.10 mmol, 50 mol%), THF (0.1 mL, 2.0 M), isopropanol (31 μL,
0.4 mmol, 200 mol%), and H2O (18 μL, 1.0 mmol, 500 mol%). But-3-en-2-yl
acetate 1 (45.6 mg, 0.40 mmol, 200 mol%) was added and the mixture was
allowed to stir at ambient temperature for 0.5 hr, at which point the
reaction vessel was placed in an oil bath at 70°C and was allowed to stir
for 48 hr. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo. Purification
of the residue by column chromatography (SiO2; ethyl acetate: hexanes,
1:20 with 0.1% TEA) provided 4f (29.0 mg, 0.154 mmol) as a colorless oil
in 77% yield (10:1 dr). HPLC: (Chiralpak AS-H/AS-H column, hexanes:i-PrOH
= 98:2, 0.5 mL/min, 254 nm), tminor = 26.8 min, tmajor = 31.5 min; ee =
98%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, oven-dried sealed tube; sixth stage pre-heated oil bath
(10:1 d.r., 98% e.e.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
