$DATUM (E)-1-(2-Thienyl)-2-penten-1-ol (±)-2i. Method A: Under a nitrogen
atmosphere, to a solution of the carbonyl compound (14 mmol) in THF (70
mL) was dropwise added the corresponding Grignard or lithium reagents (21
mmol) at -78 °C. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room
temperature and stirred until the complete consumption of the substrate.
After quenching with sat. aq. NH4Cl, the organic materials were extracted
with EtOAc. The combined organic extract was washed with brine, dried
over MgSO4, and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel) to give (±)-1 or (±)-2, using
trans-2-pentenal (600 mg, 7.1 mmol), 2-thienyllithium generated from
thiophene (900 mg, 11 mmol) and n-BuLi (1.57 M in hexanes; 6.80 mL, 11
mmol), and THF (20 mL). After 1 h at room temperature, work-up and column
chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc = 10:1) gave (±)-2i (1.10 g, 93%) as a pale
yellow oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.28-7.24 (m, 1H), 7.00-6.96 (m,
2H), 5.88 (dt, J= 15.5, 6.5 Hz, 1H), 5.74 (dd, J= 15.5, 7.0 Hz, 1H),
5.43-5.38 (m, 1H), 2.15-2.07 (m, 2H), 2.02 (br d, J= 4.0 Hz, 1H), 1.03
(t, J= 7.5 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 147.6, 134.8, 130.3,
126.7, 124.9, 123.9, 71.0, 25.0, 13.2. IR (CHCl3) ν: 3593, 3017 cm-1.
HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C9H11S [M-OH]+: 151.0576. Found: 151.0591.
