$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Methyldec-1-en-4-ol (1): Into a 0 °C
solution of heptanal (3.5 mL, 25 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was added dropwise
a solution of 2-methylallyl magnesium chloride in THF (50 mL, nominally
0.5 M). After 20 min, the reaction was quenched with water (20 mL),
acidified with conc. HCl (∼ 3 mL) and extracted with 10% EA/Hex (250 mL ×
2). The combined extracts were sequentially washed with 10% aq. HCl and
water. 3-Methyl-1-phenylbut-3-en-1-ol (15). Rf =0.3 (10% EA/Hex).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM B(C6F5)3-Promoted tandem silylation and intramolecular hydrosilylation:
diastereoselective synthesis of oxasilinanes and oxasilepanes
