$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Allylic alcohol S11: To a cooled (0°C) solution of 2-methallylmagnesium
chloride (20 mL, 0.50 M in THF, 10 mmol) was added benzaldehyde (1.01 g,
9.52 mmol) dropwise. After 1 h, the reaction mixture was diluted with
Et2O (50 mL), and H2O (50 mL) was added. The layers were separated and
the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (2 x 25 mL). The combined
organic layers were washed with H2O (25 mL) and brine (25 mL), dried over
MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography
(20:80 EtOAc:hexanes). S11 as a colorless oil (1.48 g, 96%). The spectral
data are consistent with the data reported:14. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.39-7.33 (m, 4H), 7.28-7.25 (m, 1H), 4.92 (s, 1H), 4.86 (s, 1H), 4.81
(dt, J = 6.7, 2.5, 1H), 2.42 (d, J = 6.9, 2H), 2.13-2.12 (m, 1H), 1.80
(s, 3H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 144.2 (C), 142.5 (C), 128.5 (CH),
127.6 (CH), 125.9 (CH), 114.2 (CH2), 71.5 (CH), 48.5 (CH2), 22.5 (CH3);
IR (thin film) 3382, 3073, 2969, 1647, 1493, 1374, 1054, 1028 cm-1.
