$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of racemic carbinols (±)-6: A
solution of methallylmagnesium chloride (6.6 mL, 3.0 mmol, 0.5 M in THF)
was cooled to 0 °C and benzaldehyde (0.32 g, 3.0 mmol) was added
dropwise. The cooling bath was removed and the mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 1 h after which it was quenched with 3 mL of aqueous
NH4Cl solution. The resulting mixture was washed with water (3 x 20 mL).
The organic phase was then dried over MgSO4, and the removal of solvent
in vacuo provides a pale yellow liquid. It was further purified by silica
gel column chromatography using 4:1 hexane/ether as eluent. Product as a
colorless liquid, yield 0.61 g, 94%. bp 98 °C (49 mm Hg).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Synthesis of 2°- and 3°-Carbinols via B-Methallyl-10-(TMS and
