$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Phenylpent-4-en-1-ol Magnesium turnings (1.08 g, 0.045 mol) were mixed
with Et2O (20 mL) and 4-bromo butene (3.38 g, 0.025 mol) in Et2O (10 mL)
was slowly added. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature
(rt) for 1 h and then heated to reflux for another 30 min. Then a
solution of benzaldehyde (2.33 g, 0.022 mol) in Et2O (10 mL) was slowly
added and the reaction mixture was heated to reflux for 2 h. Ice (10 g)
was added and the resulting suspension was dissolved with HCl (2 M). The
organic layer was separated, washed with aqueous NaHSO3, aqueous NaHCO3
and H2O, and dried (MgSO4). Evaporation of the solvent and distillation
at reduced pressure (bp. 125 - 127 °C / 13 mbar) afforded the desired
product as a colourless liquid (2.94 g, 82 %). 1-Phenylpent-4-en-1-ol,
yield (2.94 g, 82 %). 1H-NMR (400 MHz): δ = 7.38-7.29 (m, 5 H, aryl-H),
5.91-5.83 (m, 1 H, CH2=CH), 5.09-4.99 (m, 2 H, CH=CH2), 4.72 (dd, J1 =
7.7 Hz, J2 = 5.5 Hz, 1 H, HCO), 2.22-2.17 (m, 2 H, CH2), 2.00-1.90 (m, 3
H, OH, CH2). The physical data are in agreement with the literature
values.[1]
