$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Phenylpent-4-en-1-ol Magnesium turnings (1.08 g, 45 mmol) were mixed
with Et2O (20 mL) and 4-bromo butene (3.38 g, 25 mmol) in Et2O (10 mL)
was slowly added. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature
for 1 h and then heated to reflux for another 30 min. Then a solution of
benzaldehyde (2.33 g, 22 mmol) in Et2O (10 mL) was slowly added and the
reaction mixture was heated to reflux for 2 h. Ice (10 g) was added and
the resulting suspension was dissolved with HCl (2 M). The organic layer
was separated, washed with aqueous NaHSO3, aqueous NaHCO3 and H2O, and
dried (MgSO4). Evaporation of the solvent and distillation at reduced
pressure (bp. 125 -127 °C / 13 mbar) afforded the desired product as a
colourless liquid (2.94 g, 82 %). 1H-NMR (400 MHz): δ = 7.38-7.29 (m, 5
H), 5.91-5.83 (m, 1 H), 5.09-4.99 (m, 2 H), 4.72 (dd, J = 7.7, 5.5 Hz, 1
H), 2.22-2.17 (m, 2 H), 2.00-1.90 (m, 3 H).
