$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (R/S)-1-Phenylpent-4-en-1-ol (rac-15b) To the solution of benzaldehyde
(14b) (2.0 mL, 0.02 mol) in dry THF (30 mL) was added 2 M homoallyl
magnesium bromide solution in Et2O (9.8 mL, 0.02 mol) at -78°C. Mixture
was allowed to reach r. t. over 1 h and sat. NH4Cl solution was added,
followed by extraction with EtOAc. Organic phase was separated, washed
with brine and dried over Na2SO4. Product was purified by column
chromatography (EtOAc/ PE = 1/ 8), 1-phenylpent-4-en-1-ol (rac -15b)
(2.94 g, 92 %) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.75-1.97
(m, 3H), 2.07-2.23 (m, 2H), 4.71 (dd, J = 5.7 Hz, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 4.96-5.08
(m, 2H), 5.78-5.92 (m, 1H), 7.28-7.36 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ
30.0, 38.0, 74.0, 114.9, 125.9, 127.5, 128.4, 138.1, 144.6. In HRMS
conditions no signal observed. Data are consistent with literature2
values.
