$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Allylation of
Benzaldehyde with Substituted Allyl Bromides to Provide Products 3, 4a,
5, and 6. An oven-dried 25mLround-bottomed flask equipped with a stirbar
was cooled under argon and charged with indium powder (1 mmol),
(1S,2R)-2-amino-1,2-diphenylethanol (1 mmol), anhydrous THF (7 mL),
anhydrous pyridine (1 mmol), and allyl bromide (1 mmol). The flask was
purged with argon (4 vacuumbackfill cycles) and the mixture was stirred
vigorously at 25 °C for 30 min, at which time dry n-hexane (1 mL) was
added, the solution was cooled to -78 °C (dry ice/acetone bath), and
freshly distilled benzaldehyde (0.5 mmol) was added dropwise. After 1.5 h
the reaction was quenched with saturated ammonium chloride (1 mL) and
allowed to warm to 25 °C. The organic layer was diluted with n-hexane (5
mL), decanted, dried with anhydrous magnesium sulfate, filtered through a
small plug of silica gel ,and evaporated under reduced pressure.
3-Methyl-1-phenylbut-3-en-1-ol, 4a (Table 3, entry 2). Following the
general procedure above, 4a was obtained as a clear, colorless oil (0.057
g, 70% yield). 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.80 (s, 3H), 2.46 (d, J = 7
Hz, 2H), 4.79-4.93 (m, 3H), 7.24-7.40 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (62.9 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = 22.4, 48.4, 71.4, 114.1, 125.8, 127.5, 128.4, 142.4, 144.1.
Enantiomeric excess was determined to be 45% by chiral GC analysis. GC
conditions (for acetylated product): isothermal 120 °C, tR for (S)-isomer
48.32 min, tR for (R)-isomer 48.98 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Indium-Mediated Asymmetric Barbier-Type Allylations: Additions to
Aldehydes and Ketones and Mechanistic Investigation of the Organoindium
Reagents
