$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The reaction of 1,3-butadiene with electrophiles A 10 mL of round bottom
flask charged with InCl3 (0.442 g, 2.0 mmol) was dried by heating at 110
°C under reduced pressure (1 mmHg) for 1 h. After nitrogen was filled,
THF (2 mL) was added to dissolve InCl3. To the mixture was added Bu3SnH
(2.0 mmol) at -78 °C. The mixture was stirred for 10 min to prepare
dichloroindium hydride (HInCl2). Then 1,3-butadiene (4 mmol, measured by
volume using syringe) was added to the mixture. The solution was warmed
up to rt and stirred for 5h. Then electrophile (1.0 mmol) was added and
stirred for 3 h. The resulting mixture was quenched by 1N HCl aq (10 mL).
(When imine was used as electrophile the reaction was quenched by water.)
The reaction mixture was extracted with ether (10 mL x 3). The combined
organic layer was treated with NH4F aq and then precipitate was filtered
to remove tin compound. The filtrate was extracted with ether and dried
over MgSO4. Concentration followed by silica gel column chromatography
eluting with hexane/AcOEt = (9/1) affored product. Further Purification
was performed by distillation under reduced pressure or GPC. Product was
determined by 1H NMR. 2-Methyl-1-phenyl-but-3-en-1-ol (3k).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
