$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for catalyzed allylation:
Synthesis of 1-phenyl-but-3-en-1-ol (Table 2, entry 1).
1-phenyl-3-methyl-3-buten-1-ol (Table 2, entry 2). The procedure
described for (Table 2, entry 1) was followed using (IPr)CuF (22.4 mg,
0.047 mmol), octyltrifluorosilane (19.0 mg, 0.096 mmol),
(2-methyl-2-propenyl)triethoxysilane (310.6 mg, 1.42 mmol) and
benzaldehyde (100.0 mg, 0.942 mmol). The product was purified via
Kügelrohr distillation (chamber at 100 °C, 15 torr), affording 115.5 mg
(75%) of a colorless oil. Data was comparable to that available in the
literature.7 GC/MS, m/z: tR = 8.61 min; [M]+ calcd, 162.2; found, 162.1;
(> 95%).
