$DATUM (-)-(1S)-3-Methyl-1-phenyl-3-buten-1-ol (6Sa): A solution of
B-Methallyl-10S-trimethylsilyl-9-borabicyclo[3.3.2]decane (0.79 g, 3
mmol) in THF (3 mL) was cooled to -78 °C and benzaldehyde (0.32 g, 3.0
mmol) was added dropwise. After 1 h, the solvents were removed under
vacuum to yield 1.08 g (98%) of the corresponding borinate. The
(1R,2R)-(-)-pseudoephedrine (0.50 g, 3.0 mmol) and acetonitrile (7 mL)
were added and the mixture was heated at reflux temperature for 2 h and
slowly cooled to room temperature resulting in large crystals. The
crystals were separated and washed with pentane (3 x 10 mL) to yield 0.84
g (75%) of
9-(1R,2R-Pseudoephedrinyl)-(10S)-trimethylsilyl-9-borabicyclo[3.3.2]decane.
The residue was distilled. (-)-(1S)-3-Methyl-1-phenyl-3-buten-1-ol, yield
0.39 g, 80%. (bp 95 °C at 48 mm Hg). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 1.81 (s,
3H), 2.15 (s, 1H), 2.47 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H), 4.83 (dd, app t, J = 6.7 Hz,
1H), 4.93 (dd, app d, J =19.7 Hz, 2H), 6.75-7.41 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) δ 22.3, 48.2, 71.4, 113.9, 125.7, 127.4, 128.3, 142.3, 144.0.
[α]D23= -42.2 (c = 9.90, CHCl3, 95% ee).
