$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedures for addition of
phenylacethylene to aldehydes: All manipulations were carried out under
argon atmosphere using dried and degassed solvent. The ligand 7 (8.1mg,
0.025mmol) and Ti(OiPr)4 (27.4µL, 0.1mmol) were mixed in dry CH2Cl2 at
room temperature. Then, a solution of Et2Zn (1.0 M in CH2Cl2, 0.75mL) was
added. After the mixture was stirred at the room temperature for 2h,
phenylacetylene(82.4µL, 0.75mmol) was added and the stirring continued
for 1h. The yellow solution was cooled to 0°C and treated with
aldehyde(0.25mmol), then the resultant mixture was allowed to warm up to
room temperature and stirred for 12-14h. After the reaction was
completed, checked by TLC, it was cooled to 0°C and quenched by 5%
aqueous HCl. The mixture was extracted with ether. The organic layer was
washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated under vacuum. The
residue was purified by flash column chromatography (silica gel, 12.5%
EtOAc in hexane). The product. 1,5-Diphenyl-pent-1-en-4-yl-3-ol: 71%
yield. 93% ee detemined by HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD column,
IPA:hexane=1:10). Retention time: tmajor=22.58 min, tminor=71.62 min.
[α]18 D= +1 (c=2.58, CHCl3). 1H NMR(200MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.47-7.23(m, 10H),
6.88-6.80(d, J=15.8Hz, 1H). 6.33-6.26(m, 1H), 5.28(d, J=5.6Hz, 1H),
2.04(s, 1H). (Gao, G.; Moore, D.; Xie, R. G.; Pu, L. Org. Lett. 2002, 4,
4143)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, in-situ generated catalyst in the first stage
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
