$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (E)-2,4-Dimethylhepta-1,4-dien-3-ol. The
Grignard reagent prepared from 2-bromopropene (1.53 g, 12.8 mmol) and Mg
powder (123 mg, 14.3 mmol) in THF (50 mL) was cooled to 0 °C.
2-Methyl-2-pentenal (1.05 g, 10.7 mmol) was added dropwise as a solution
in THF (5 mL). After stirring at 0 °C for 30 min, the reaction was
quenched with water. The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was
extracted with ether (2 × 50 mL). The organic phases were combined,
washed with brine (50 mL), dried over MgSO4 and concentrated.
Purification by flash chromatography (1:10 EtOAc/hexanes, 60 g of silica
gel, 20 × 3 cm column). (E)-2,4-Dimethyl-1-phenylpenta-1,4-dien-3-ol.
Colorless oil, yield 86%. Rf 0.23 (1:9 EtOAc/hexanes); IR (film) 3337,
3077, 2988, 1647, 1490, 1446, 1373, 1057, 902, 753, 698 cm-1; 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.38-7.18 (m, 5 H), 6.61 (br s, 1 H), 5.15 (br s, 1 H),
4.99 (br s, 1 H), 4.59 (br s, 1 H), 1.91 (br s, 1 H), 1.78 (d, 3 H, J =
1.5 Hz), 1.69 (s, 3 H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 145.27, 137.99,
137.74, 129.14, 128.31, 126.87, 126.69, 111.80, 81.15, 18.68, 13.59;
Anal. Calcd for C13H16O: C, 82.94; H, 8.57. Found: C, 82.78; H, 8.52.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formal Intermolecular 4 + 4 Approach to Cyclooctanoids: 4 + 3 Capture of
the Nazarov Oxyallyl Intermediate with Simple 1,3-Dienes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Yong; Schill, Brenden D.; Arif, Atta M.; West, F. G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2003), 5(15), 2747-2750

