$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (2): (+/-)-(1E)-2-Methyl-1-phenylhex-1-en-5-yn-3-ol (General Procedure A)
In situ procedure: B-Br-9-BBN A 25 mL round bottom flask was flame dried
under a stream of nitrogen and allowed to cool to rt. To this was added
B-Bromo-9-BBN (2.4 mL, 2.4 mmol) and the temperature was subsequently
decreased to -78 °C. Freshly prepared allenyl magnesium bromide (0.77 M
in ether, 3.1 mL, 2.4 mmol) was added dropwise. After 2 h at -78 °C the
cooling bath was removed and the reaction warmed to rt. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 30 min5 and then α-methyl-trans-cinnamaldehyde
(223 µL, 1.6 mmol) was added dropwise via syringe. After 1 h the reaction
mixture was cooled to 0 °C and 3 N NaOH (3 mL) followed by 30% H2O2 (3
mL, warning! vigorous exotherm and evolution of gas, slow addition and
appropriate venting is recommended) were added. The reaction was stirred
at rt for 3 h after which time it was diluted with ether and washed with
a saturated solution of NH4Claq. The aqueous layer was back extracted
with ether, the combined organics dried with MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue was purified by flash
chromatography (10 to 17% EtOAc/Hex) to afford the product (2) as a
colorless oil (295 mg, yield = 99%). R f = 0.19 (17% EtOAc/Hex); 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.32 - 7.22 (m, 4H), 7.21 - 7.16 (m, 1H), 6.55 (s,
1H), 4.32 (dd, J = 6.4, 6.4 Hz, 1H), 2.72 (brs, 1H), 2.52 (dd, J = 6.4,
