$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (2): (+/-)-(1E)-2-Methyl-1-phenylhex-1-en-5-yn-3-ol (General Procedure A)
A dry 25 mL round bottom flask was charged with B-allenyl-9-BBN (0.8 M in
ether, 3 mL, 2.4 mmol) and diluted with freshly distilled THF (3 mL). To
the resulting light yellow solution was added
α-methyl-trans-cinnamaldehyde (223 µL, 1.6 mmol) over approximately 1 min
resulting in a noticeable exotherm. After 1 h the reaction mixture was
cooled to 0 °C and 3 N NaOH (3 mL) followed by 30% H2O2 (3 mL, warning!
vigorous exotherm and evolution of gas, slow addition and appropriate
venting is recommended) were added. The reaction was stirred at rt for 3
h after which time it was diluted with ether and washed with a saturated
solution of NH4Claq. The aqueous layer was back extracted with ether, the
combined organics dried with MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
The crude residue was purified by flash chromatography (10 to 17%
EtOAc/Hex) to afford the product (2) as a colorless oil (295 mg, yield =
99%). R f = 0.19 (17% EtOAc/Hex); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.32 - 7.22
(m, 4H), 7.21 - 7.16 (m, 1H), 6.55 (s, 1H), 4.32 (dd, J = 6.4, 6.4 Hz,
1H), 2.72 (brs, 1H), 2.52 (dd, J = 6.4, 2.8 Hz, 2H), 2.05 (dd, J = 2.8,
2.8 Hz, 1H), 1.84 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 138.3,
137.4, 129.1, 128.2, 126.7, 126.6, 80.9, 75.7, 71.1, 26.1, 13.6; FTIR
(neat) ν 3293, 3296, 2917, 1600, 1492, 1446, 1018, 920 cm-1; HRMS (m/z)
calculated for C13H14O1 (EI, M+) 186.1045, found 186.1049.
