$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Addition of Ph2Zn to
aldehyde To a solution of chiral ligand 3f (9.2 mg, 0.025 mmol) in
toluene (5 ml) was added diphenylzinc (110 mg, 0.5 mmol) at room
temperature and the mixture was stirred at room temperature for 15 min.
Aldehyde (0.25 mmol) was added in one portion at 0°C and the reaction
mixture was stirred for 1h at 0°C. The reaction was quenched by the
addition of 1M HCl solution (10 ml) and the mixture was extRacted with
ethyl acetate (20 ml x 2). The combined organic extRacts were washed with
brine (20 ml x 2), dried (MgSO4), and concentRated in vacuo. The residue
was purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel with ethyl
acetate/hexanes (1:7) to give the pure alcohol product.
(4-Methoxyphenyl)phenylmethanol 1,3-Diphenyl-prop-2-en-1-ol yeild 93%.
[α]D25 = -17.55 (c = 1.1, CH2Cl2) {lit.7 [α]D 27 = +28.1 (c = 1.0,
CH2Cl2) for 82% ee (R) }; 75% ee by HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD column,
hexane:2-propanol = 9:1, 1 ml/min, 254 nm UV detector), tR = 17.63 min
for (R) and tR = 13.38 min for (S).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective additions of diethylzinc and diphenylzinc to aldehydes
using 2-dialkylaminomethyl-2'-hydroxy-1,1'-binaphthyls
