$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (B) General Procedure for Asymmetric Addition
of Arylboronic Acid to Aldehydes To a Schlenk tube was charged with
[RhCl(CH2CH2)2]2 (0.37 mg, 1 mol %) and ligand (S)-1g (1.7 mg,2.1 equiv
to Rh) and 1 mL toluene, and the mixture was stirred at room temperature
for 30 min before cooled to 0 °C. ArB(OH)2 (0.38 mmol), KF (22 mg, 0.38
mmol), water (1 mL) and aldehyde (0.19 mmol) was added sequentially. The
mixture was stirred for appropriate time at 0 °C (monitored by TLC) and
was extracted with CH2Cl2, dried over MgSO4. The product was purified by
chromatography on silica gel with petroleum ether/ethyl acetate and
subjected to analysis of enantiomerical excess by chiral HPLC.
(S)-1,3-Diphenyl-prop-2-en-1-ol (9i). 96% yield, [α]D20 = -23.1 (c 0.68,
CH2Cl2), 75% ee (lit.7 [α]D27 = +28.1 (c 1.0, CH2Cl2) for 82% ee, (R)),
[HPLC condition: Chiralcel OD-H column, n-hexane/2-propanol = 90:10, 1.0
ml/min, 254 nm UV detector, tR = 13.41 min for (S) and tR = 17.40 min for
(R)]. 1H NMR δ 7.44-7.24 (m, 10H, Ar-H), 6.69 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H, CH),
6.39 (dd, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H, CH), 5.38 (s, 1H, CH), 2.11 (br s, 1H, OH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 75% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Rhodium-Catalyzed Addition of Arylboronic Acids to
Aldehydes Using Chiral Spiro Monophosphite Ligands
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Duan, Hai-Feng; Xie, Jian-Hua; Shi, Wen-Jian; Zhang, Qi; Zhou, Qi-Lin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(7), 1479-1481

