$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Phenyl Transfer
Reaction and typical recycling procedure. A solution of the
triphenylcyclotriboroxane (0.5 equiv) and diethylzinc (4.5 equiv) in
toluene was stirred at 60 °C for 4 h then cooled to 0 °C, and ligand was
then added. The mixture was cooled to -15 °C, and then the aldehyde (1.0
equiv) was subsequently added. After being stirred for 6 h at -15 °C, dry
methanol was added to precipitate the dendritic catalyst and the solution
was filtered and purified by silica gel chromatography [SiO2,
EtOAc-petroleum ether (1: 20)] to give the diarylmethanol. The dendritic
catalyst was extracted by DCM. And, then the solution was removed diary
methanol. And the next reaction could be conducted.
(R)-(E)-1,3-Diphenyl-2-propenol 16i: 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.28 (br
s, 1H), 5.35 (d, J = 7Hz, 1H), 6.37 (dd, J = 7 Hz, J = 16 Hz, 1H), 6.65
(d, J = 16Hz, 1H), 7.29-7.41 (m, 10H); HPLC-separation condChiralcel OD,
19 °C, 254 nm, 90: 10 hexane/i-PrOH, 1 mL/min; t R = 20.5 min (S), tR =
26.4 min (R).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly effective and recyclable dendritic ligands for the
enantioselective aryl transfer reactions to aldehydes
