$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the addition of
arylboronic acids to aldehydes (Table. 2): (acac)Rh(coe)2 (0.03 mmol) and
arylboronic acid (2.0 mmol) were added to a 20 mL-flask containing a
magnetic stirring bar, a septum inlet, and a reflux condenser. The flask
was flushed with argon and then charged with DME (3 mL), (tert-Bu3)P
(0.03 mmol), water (2 mL), and aldehyde (1.0 mmol) with a syringe through
the septum inlet. After being stirred stirred for 16 h at room
temperature (25-28 °C), the product was extracted with benzene, washed
with brine, dried over MgSO4 , and isolated by column chromatography over
silica geL The general procedure gave following compounds shown in Table
2. 3-Nitrophenyl(phenyl)methanol (entry 1). The general procedure gave
239 mg (94%) of the title compound as a white solid; 1,2-Addition to
trans-cinnamaldehyde (1,3-Dipheny1-2-propen-1-ol in Scheme 2). The
general procedure for Table 2 gave 189 mg (90%) of the title compound as
a clear oil; IR (neat) 3340, 3010, 1600, 1595, 1548 cm-1 ; 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3 ) δ 2.11 (brs, 1H), 5.37 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 1H), 6.37 (dd, J =
6.5, 15.9 Hz, 1H), 6.68 (d, J = 15.9 Hz, 1H), 7.20-7.43 (m, 10H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3 ) δ 75.1, 126.3, 126.6, 127.8, 128.3, 128.5, 128.6,
130.5, 131.5, 136.5, 142.7; exact mass calcd for C 15H14O, 210.1045,
