$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Copper Fluoride
Catalyzed Cyanomethylation by TMSCH2CN (Table 1, entry 6): To a solution
of CuF·3PPh3·2EtOH (9.6 mg, 0.01 mmol) in THF (0.4 mL), 2f (58.5 mg, 0.40
mmol) and (EtO)3SiF (89 mL, 0.48 mmol) were added in an ice bath. To the
mixed solution, TMSCH2CN (66 mL, 0.48 mmol) was added slowly over 1 h by
a syringe pump. After 6 h, 3HF·NEt3 (0.3 mL) was added for desilylation
(ca. 1 h). Satd. NaCl was added and the product was extracted with AcOEt.
The combined organic layer was washed with satd. NaHCO3, and dried over
Na2SO4. Filtration, evaporation, and purification through silica gel
column chromatography (AcOEt/hexane = 1/3∼1/2). Entry 10, yield 92%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, slow addn. of TMSCH2CN important for high yields
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct Catalytic Aldol-Type Reactions Using RCH2CN
