$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedures for the Asymmetric Aryl
Addition of Aldehydes. Synthesis of (R)-Naphthalen-1-yl-phenyl-methanol
(4a). Under a dry nitrogen atmosphere, [{(R)-H8-BINOLate}Ti(O-i- Pr)2]n28
(0.023 g, 0.050 mmol) and Ti(O-i-Pr)4 (0.22 mL, 0.75 mmol) were mixed in
4.0 mL of dry toluene at room temperature. After stirring for 30 min,
AlPhEt2(THF) (0.70 mmol) was added at 0 °C. The mixture was stirred for
another 10 min, and the resulting solution was treated with
1-naphaldehyde (0.068 mL, 0.50 mmol) at 0 °C. The mixture was allowed to
react at this temperature and then quenched with 2 M NaOH. The aqueous
phase was extracted with diethyl ether (3 × 10 mL), dried over MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated. The residue was purified by column
chromatography to give the secondary alcohol 4a. 12.
(S)-(E)-1,3-Diphenyl-prop-2-en-1-ol (4l) (Table 2, Entry 12, 91 % ee)4
Catalytic Reaction Conditions: (E)-PhCH=CHCHO: 0.5 mmol,
(R)-H8-BINOLateTi(O-i-Pr)4: 0.05 mmol, Ti(O-i-Pr)4: 0.625 mmol,
AlPhEt2(THF): 0.7 mmol, toluene: 4 mL, 0 °C, 1 h, yield 93% Spectra data:
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.45-7.22 (m, 10H), 6.67 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H),
6.42-6.36 (m, 1H), 5.39 (dd, J = 3.2 Hz and 6.8 Hz, 1H), 2.07 (d, J = 3.6
Hz, 1H). 13C{1H} NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 142.7, 136.5, 131.5, 130.5,
128.6, 128.5, 127.7, 126.6, 126.3, 75.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Enantioselective Arylation of Aldehydes and Ketones Using
AlArEt2(THF) as Aryl Sources
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
