$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-3-Hydroxy-5-phenylpent-4-enenitrile (3dj) [110729-74-3]: AcOLi (1.6
mg, 0.025 mmol) was placed in a flask. After the atmosphere of the
reaction flask was replaced with argon, 2j (67.1 mg, 0.508 mmol) and DMF
(1.0 mL) were introduced to the flask via syringes and stirred. Nitrile
1d (64.7 mg, 0.652 mmol) was added to the stirred solution at 0 °C. After
24 h MeOH (5 mL) and 1 M aqueous HCl (5 mL) were added to the reaction
mixture and stirred for 10 min. The resultant mixture was extracted with
AcOEt (4x10 mL). The combined organic layer was washed with saturated
aqueous NaCl, dried over Na2SO4, and evaporated. Purification of the
crude product (silica-gel column chromatography; hexane/AcOEt = 2:1) gave
(E)-3-hydroxy-5-phenylpent-4-enenitrile (3dj). Yield 73.9 mg, 0.427 mmol,
84%. MF = C11H11NO. MW = 173.21. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.29 (br. s,
1H), 2.68 (dd, J = 16.5, 6.0 Hz, 1H), 2.70 (dd, J = 16.5, 5.7 Hz, 1H),
4.60-4.68 (m, 1H), 6.25 (dd, J = 15.9, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 6.72 (d, J = 15.9 Hz,
1H), 7.27-7.42 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ. 26.3, 68.7, 117.1,
126.7 (CH x 2), 127.9, 128.5, 128.7 (CH x 2), 133.1, 135.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nucleophilic Addition of α-(Dimethylsilyl)nitriles to Aldehydes and
Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
