$DATUM 1-(Cyclobut-1-en-1-yl)-3-methylbutan-1-ol To a -78 °C solution of
1-bromocyclobut-1-ene13 (1.6 M in Et2O, 5.0 mL, 8.0 mmol) was added
dropwise t-BuLi (1.9 M in pentane, 8.4 mL, 16.0 mmol) over a 5-10 min
period. The mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 2 h. After this time,
isovaleradehyde (690 μL, 6.4 mmol) was added in one portion to the
reaction mixture. The cold bath was removed and the temperature was
allowed to warm to RT and stirred for 1.5 h. The reaction mixture was
then diluted with Et2O and quenched with a saturated aqueous NH4Cl
solution. The aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O, and the combined
organic extracts were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel (95 : 5 / PE : EtOAc). The desired product
as a pale yellow oil (630 mg, 70%); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 5.84 (br.
s, 1H), 4.15-4.09 (m, 1H), 2.49-2.45 (m, 2H), 2.36-2.32 (m, 2H),
1.82-1.70 (m, 1H), 1.59-1.31 (m, 3H), 0.98 (2*d, 6H, J = 6.5 Hz); 13C NMR
(100.2 Mz, CDCl3) δ 151.9, 127.7, 68.3, 44.3, 28.4, 26.3, 24.5, 23.3,
22.2; FTIR (CCl4, νmax cm-1): 3619 (m), 2957 (s), 2924 (s), 1467 (m),
1367 (m); HMRS (EI): m/z [M-H2O]+ calcd C9H14 122.1096, found 122.1094.
