$DATUM The Grignard reagent in THF solution (6 mmol, 0.5 M, 12 mL) was prepared
according to the literature from 5- bromopent-1-ene and Magnesium. At 0
°C, the Grignard was added in to benzylaldehyde THF solution (5 mmol, 0.5
M 10 ml), under argon atmosphere. The reaction mixture was gradually
warmed to room temperature and stirred for an additional 4 hours. Next,
HCl aqueous solution (5 mL, 1.0 M) was added slowly to quench the
reaction. The mixture was diluted with EtOAc (200 mL) and washed by
saturated NaHCO3 (aq.) and brine and then dried over anhydrous Na2SO4.
The solvent was removed under reduced pressure to give the crude residue.
Flash silica gel chromatography (Ethyl Acetate/Hexane 20:80) afforded
alcohol. Yield 836 mg, 95%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
