$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of alcohols IIa-c. A sample of the
corresponding bromoalkene I (1.0 mmol) was added to a mixture of Mg (1.2
mmol) in THF (10 mL) and stirred for 30 min. Benzaldehyde (1.0 mmol) was
then added and the resulting mixture was stirred for 1 h at room
temperature. The reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc, washed with
saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and the
solvent removed. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
(EtOAc/Hexane mixtures) yielding the corresponding alcohols II, which
showed NMR spectra identical to those reported: IIa4.
