$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Rel-(3R, 5R)-deca-4,5-dien-3-ol (3):
MMD-coordinated octa-2,3-dienal 2 (0.558 g, 1.6 mmol) was dissolved in
dry ether (16.0 mL, 0.1 M) and cooled to -40°C (acetonitrile/dry ice
bath) for 10 minutes. To this solution, ethyl magnesium bromide (1.20 mL,
3.5 mmol, 3M) was added drop wise (over 5 min) and the resulting reaction
mixture was allowed to stir at -40°C. The reaction was monitored by TLC.
After completion (~1 h), the reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous
NH4Cl solution (5 mL) and extracted with diethyl ether (3×30 mL). The
combined ether layers were dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated under reduced
pressure. The crude product was dissolved again in dry acetone (20 mL)
under an argon atmosphere and treated with PhI(OAc)2 (1.03 g, 3.20 mmol).
After ~2.0 h (completion of reaction determined by TLC), the solvent was
removed by evaporation. The crude product (now decomplexed) was purified
by silica gel flash chromatography using 10% EtOAc/hexanes.
Rel-(1R,3R)-1-phenylocta-2,3-dien-1-ol (8): Prepared according to the
general procedure; (0.246 g, 76%) as a light yellow viscous liquid. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.37-7.23 (m, 5H), 5.38-5.34 (m, 1H), 5.33-5.21
(m, 1H), 5.20 -5.22 (m, 1H), 2.02-1.98 (m, 2H), 1.36-1.29 (m, 4H), 0.86
(t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H).; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 202.4, 143.3, 128.4,
127.6, 126.1, 96.1, 94.7, 72.5, 31.2, 28.4, 22.2, 14.0; HRMS calc. for
C14H18O [M+H]+: 203.14. Found: 203.1430.
