$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Hydroxy-2-methylene-octa-trans,trans-4,6-dienoic acid methyl ester
(isomeric mixture) (7). To a stirring solution of DABCO (13.2 g, 117.8
mmol) and trans,trans-2,4-hexadienal (6.5 mL, 58.9 mmol) in MeOH (30 mL)
at 0°C in an ice-water bath was added methyl acrylate (15.9 mL, 176.7
mmol). The solution was stirred at 0-5°C for 3 days before being quenched
with 0.5 M HCl (30 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (5 x 30 mL). The organic
layers were washed with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (30 mL) followed by
brine (30 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
resulting yellow oil was purified by column chromatography (SiO2, 1:10
EtOAc/hexanes increased to 1:4 EtOAc/hexanes) to afford yellow oil 7
(7.58 g, 41.6 mmol, 70%). Compound 7 was isolated as a 85:15 mixture of
geometrical isomers. The peaks listed below correspond to the major
isomer. 3-Hydroxy-2-methylene-octa-trans,trans-4,6-dienoic acid methyl
ester, yield (7.58 g, 41.6 mmol, 70%). Rf = 0.4 (1:2 EtOAc/hexanes). 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): 6.25 (dd, J=10.6, 14.9, 1H), 6.20 (s, 1H), 6.05
(ddd, J=1.3, 10.9, 14.6, 1H), 5.85 (s, 1H), 5.75 (dd, J=6.8, 13.7, 1H),
5.62 (dd, J=6.7, 15.2, 1H), 4.98 (t, J=5.8, 1H), 3.75 (s, 3H), 2.85 (d,
J=5.9, 1H), 1.73 (d, J=6.7, 3H). 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, CDCl3): 167.0,
141.6, 132.2, 130.9, 130.8, 130.1, 125.7, 72.1, 52.2, 18.4. HRMS: (EI)
calcd for C10H14O3 (M+), 182.0943; found: 182.0948. IR (neat): 3421 (br),
1719 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 85:15 mixture of gamma,delta-olefin isomers,
Morita-Baylis-Hillman reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis and Cytoprotective Properties of Dykellic Acid
