$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1-(Benzofuran-2-yl)prop-2-en-1-ol (34a). To a
flame-dried, round-bottomed flask, underan argon atmosphere, added
benzofuran-2-carbaldehyde (1.24 mL, 10.2 mmol) and ether (20 mL). Placed
in an ice bath and added a 1.0 M THF solution of vinylmagnesium bromide
(20.4 mL, 20.4 mmol) dropwise. Removed ice bath shortly thereafter and
let stir at room temperature for 2 hours. Slowly added 50 mL aqueous
NH4Cl solution, extracted 3 times with 20 mL ether, and dried with
Na2SO4. Purified via silica gel chromatography (8:2 pentane:ether).
1-(Thiophen-2-yl)prop-2-en-1-ol, yellow oil, yield 92%. 1H NMR (300
MHz,CDCl3, ppm): δ 7.55 (1H, m), 7.27 (2H, m), 6.41 (1H, ddd, J = 17.2,
10.3, 5.9 Hz), 5.7(2H, m), 5.53 (1H, dt, J = 10.5, 1.2 Hz), 2.47 (1H,
br). 13C NMR (75.4 MHz, CDCl3,ppm): δ 146.8, 139.5, 127.0, 125.5, 124.6,
116.0, 71.2. HRMS (EI) calcd. for C7H7OS:140.0296, found: 140.0291.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rhenium-Catalyzed 1,3-Isomerization of Allylic Alcohols: Scope and
Chirality Transfer
