$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
anti-Homopropargyl Alcohols via Kinetic Resolution-Allenylboration With
(±)-1: To a vial was sequentially added (R)-TRIP-PA ((R)-2, 10 mol%),
powdered 4Å MS (~100 mg), aldehyde if solid (0.2 mmol) and a stir bar.
The reaction was sealed and purged with Ar. Toluene (1 mL) was then added
followed by aldehyde if liquid (0.2 mmol). The suspension was stirred at
amibient temperature for 15 min and cooled to -50 °C. Allenylboronate
(±)-12 (0.56 mmol, 2.8 equiv) was then added dropwise. The reaction
mixture was then stirred at -50 °C for 16 h. The mixture was then warmed
to room temperature, filtered through a plug of Celite and washed with
EtOAc. To the filtrate was added sat. aq NaHCO3 (~0.5 mL) and the two
phase mixture was stirred vigorously for 30 minutes. The layers were then
separated and the aqueous layer then extracted with EtOAc (2 x 5 mL). The
combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4, then filtered and
concentrated on a rotary evaporator. The crude oil was then purified by
column chromatography (10:1 to 3:1 hexane: diethyl ether) to obtain the
pure product. (3S,4R)-4-methyl-1-phenylhept-5-yn-3-ol (3a). Prepared
according to the general procedure above with hydrocinnamaldehyde to
yield a oil. (3S,4R, E)-4-methyl-1-phenylhept-1-en-5-yn-3-ol (3b).
Prepared according to the general procedure above with cinnamaldehyde to
yield a oil. Colorless oil, (95%); 20:1 ds; 95% ee. [α]D 27 = +36 (c 0.8,
CHCl3) [literature data2 for the (3R,4S)-enantiomer enantiomer: [α]D 28 =
-42.8 (c 0.9, CHCl3)] The spectroscopic data for this compound were in
agreement with previously reported data.2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chiral Bronsted acid catalyzed enantioselective synthesis of
anti-homopropargyl alcohols via kinetic resolution-aldehyde
allenylboration using racemic allenylboronates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tsai, Andy S.; Chen, Ming; Roush, William R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(7), 1568-1571

