$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (E)-1-(4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)non-2-en-1-ol
(20). Step 1: To a flame-dried, roundbottomed flask, under an argon
atmosphere, added 1-octyne (6.5 mL, 44 mmol) and ether (120 mL). Placed
in a dry ice/acetone bath and let stir for approximately 10 minutes.Added
a 1.6 M hexanes solution of n-butyllithium (24 mL, 38 mmol) dropwise and
let stirat -78 °C for 30 minutes. Added, at -78 °C, a solution of
α,α,α-trifluoro-p-tolualdehyde(4 mL, 30 mmol) and ether (30 mL) dropwise.
Let stir at -78 °C for 1 hour, then removed dry ice/acetone bath and let
slowly warm to room temperature. Quenched by slow addition of 100 mL
aqueous NH4Cl solution, extraction 3 times with 100 mL ether, and drying
with Na2SO4. Purified via silica gel chromatography (7:3 pentane:ether).
(E)-3-methyl-1-phenylnon-2-en-1-ol, yield 820 mg, 72%.
