$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Phenyl-3-buten-1-ol (representative
procedure): A mixture of benzaldehyde (530 mg, 5.0 mmol), allyl bromide
(0.88 g, 8 mmol) and stannous chloride (2.25 g, 10 mmol) in water (10 mL)
was stirred in a 10 mL round bottom flask cell equipped with paired
graphite electrode at room temperature. The suspension was electrolyzed
at constant potential (2.0 v) on a graphite anode (dia. 6 mm) and a
graphite cathode (dia. 6 mm) and was stirred alternately until
benzaldehyde was transformed throughly with the reaction time 6-10 h (or
2 F mol-1 of current was consumed under 100 mA constant current with the
electrolysis time 2-3 h). Afterwards, the reaction mixture was extracted
with ether (3×25 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over
anhydrous sodium sulfate and the organic solvent was removed on a rotary
evaporator. The residue afforded the corresponding homoallylic alcohols
with sufficient purity as judged by TLC and1H NMR without the need for
further purification. 1-(4-methylphenyl)-3-buten-1-ol. 1H NMR (300Hz,
CDCl3): δ 2.02-2.19 (br, 1H), 2.33 (s, 3H), 2.48 (dd, J=6.58, 6.92 Hz,
2H), 4.67 (t, J=6.49 Hz, 1H), 5.07-5.19 (m, 2H), 5.70-5.87 (m, 1H ), 7.14
(d, J=7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.22 (d, J=7.80 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (75Hz, CDCl3): δ
21.2, 43.8, 73.7, 118.2, 125.9, 129.2, 134.8, 137.2, 141.1. IR (film):
3383, 3075, 1640 cm-1. HRMS (EI) calc. for C11H12 (M+-H2O) 144.0939,
found 144.0924.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM electrochemical, green chemistry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A recyclable electrochemical allylation in water
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zha, Zhenggen; Hui, Ailing; Zhou, Yuqing; Miao, Qian; Wang, Zhiyong;
Zhang, Hanchang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2005), 7(10), 1903-1905

