$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure for the NHK Reaction
of Allyl Halides with Aldehydes 25 Catalyzed by (+)-12: To an oven dried
vial were added molecular sieves (3 Å), Mn powder (325 mesh, 21 mg, 0.38
mmol) and a catalytic amount of chromium complex (+)-12 (8.3 mg, 12.61
μmol, 10 mol%) and the vial was flushed with argon for 15 min. To the
mixture was added anhydrous THF (1 mL) and the resulting brown suspension
was stirred at room temperature for 2 h. The suspension was treated with
allyl bromide or chloride (0.19 mmol) and the mixture was stirred for 1
h. To this mixture was added neat aldehyde 25 (0.12 mmol) and TMSCl (24
μL, 0.19 mmol) at the temperature specified in Table 3 and the mixture
was stirred at that temperature for the specified length of time. The
reaction was quenched with saturated NaHCO3 solution (1 mL), volatiles
were removed in vacuo, and the residue was extracted with ether (2 x 10
mL). The extract was washed with brine (20 mL), dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated under reduced pressure, and the resulting crude silyl ether
was treated with aqueous HCl (1M, 2 mL, 2 mmol) in THF (2 mL) at room
temperature until desilylation was complete by TLC. The mixture was
diluted with Et2O (20 mL), and the solution was washed with brine (20
mL), dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel (30%
hexane/ether). The enantiomeric excess of the pure product was determined
by HPLC on a Daicel Chiralcel OD column. (S)-1-Phenylbut-3-en-1-ol (28a)
(S)-1-p-Tolylbut-3-en-1-ol (28c) Pale yellow oil: 95% ee [Chiralcel OD,
hexane:i-propanol 98.5:1.5, 0.5 mL/min tR (minor) 21.7 min, tR (major)
28.6 min]; [α]D 20 - 66.5 (c 0.1, CH2Cl2), [lit.13 for R enantiomer [α]D
25 + 53.0 (c 1.0, CHCl3, 78% ee)]; IR (neat) 3332, 3074, 2922, 2860,
1638, 1606, 1513, 1435, 1295, 1260, 1245, 1182, 1112, 1046, 999, 914,
871, 813, 754, 711 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.38 (s, 3H), 2.52 (m,
2H), 4.71 (m, 1H), 5.18 (m, 2H), 6.82 (m, 1H), 7.17 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H),
7.28 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (175 MHz, CDCl3) δ 21.3, 43.8, 73.2,
118.6, 125.8, 129.1, 134.3, 137.3, 140.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, molecular sieves used
