$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-p-Tolyl-3-buten-1-ol (1h)3,8 Following the
Representative Procedure, 4-methylbenzaldehyde (120 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130 μL, 1.2
mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30 psi of CO
at 70 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with pentane/MTBE (4:1, 300 mL) provided 1h (138
mg, 85%) as a colorless oil. 1-p-Tolyl-3-buten-1-ol (1h)3,8, yield 138
mg, 85%. Data for 1h: 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.25 (d, J = 8.1, 2 H,
Aryl) 7.16 (d, J = 8.1, 2 H, Aryl), 5.80 (ddt, J = 17.3, 10.1, 7.2, 1 H,
HC(3)), 5.16-5.13 (m, 2 H, H2C(4)), 4.70 (td, J = 5.2, 2.2, 1 H, HC(1)),
2.50 (m, 2 H, H2C(2)), 2.34 (s, 3 H, H3C(7')), 2.05 (d, J = 2.2, 1 H, OH)
13C NMR: (125 MHz, CDCl3) 140.9 (C(1')), 137.2 (C(3)), 134.6 (C(4')),
129.1 (C(2'), C(6')), 125.7 (C(3'), C(5')), 118.2 (C(4)), 73.51 (C(1)),
43.7 (C(7')), 21.1 (C(2)) IR: (NaCl) 3390 (m), 3071 (m), 3014 (m), 2976
(m), 2921 (s), 2857 (m), 1640 (m), 1514 (m), 1431 (m), 1306 (m), 1119 (m)
HRMS: (CI) Calcd. for C11H15O, 163.1123; found, 163.1126 TLC: Rf 0.23
(hexanes/MTBE, 4:1) [UV, CAM]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
