$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-(Thiophen-2-yl)-3-buten-1-ol (1m)5,8 Following the
Representative Procedure, 2-thiophenecarboxaldehyde (112 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130 μL, 1.2
mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30 psi of CO
at 70 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with pentane/MTBE (10:1, 100 mL; 4:1, 200 mL);
solvent was removed in rotavap at 5-10 °C (25 torr) provided 1m (127 mg,
84%) as a colorless oil. 1-(Thiophen-2-yl)-3-buten-1-ol (1m)5,8, yield
127 mg, 84%. Data for 1m: 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.26 (m , 1 H, Aryl),
6.98 (m, 2 H, Aryl), 5.88-5.77 (m, 1 H, HC(3)), 5.23-5.16 (m, 2 H,
H2C(4)), 5.00-4.95 (m, 1 H, HC(1)), 2.65-2.59 (m, 2 H, H2C(2)), 2.32 (br,
1 H, HO) 13C NMR: (125 MHz, CDCl3) 147.7 (C(1')), 133.8 (C(3)), 126.5
(C(4')), 124.4 (C(3')), 123.6 (C(2')), 118.7 (C(4)), 69.3 (C(1)), 43.7
(C(2)) IR (NaCl) 3390 (s), 3075 (m), 2978 (m), 2905 (m), 1704 (m), 1641
(m), 1435 (m), 1315 (m), 1229 (m), 1035 (s) HRMS (CI) Calcd. for C8H11OS,
155.0531; found, 155.0533 TLC: Rf 0.29 (hexanes/MTBE, 4:1) [UV, CAM]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
