$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of aldehyde (1 mmol) in 1.35 mL
of anhydrous DMF was added trichloroacetic acid (1.5 mmol) and sodium
trichloroacetate (1.5 mmol) with stirring at room temperature. Initially
rapid evolution of CO2 was observed. After 3-6 hours the mixture was
diluted with 5 mL of diethyl ether and washed with saturated aqueous
sodium bicarbonate. Precipitated solids were filtered and washed three
times with diethyl ether. The filtrate was washed two more times with
sodium bicarbonate solution and once with brine. The organic phase was
dried with sodium sulfate and the diethyl ether was evaporated under
reduced pressure. The resulting residue was eluted through a plug of
silica gel with 95:5 hexane/ethyl acetate. The crude material was
purified by silica gel flash chromatography using 95:5 hexane/EtOAc as
eluent. 1,1,1-Trichloro-4,8-dimethylnona-3,7-dien-2-ol, yield 78%.
Slightly yellow crystals as a 1:5 mixture of E/Z diastereomers. m.p.
41-42 °C. Z: 1H NMR (CDCl3, 360 MHz) δ 5.36 (dd, 1H), 5.09 (m, 1H), 4.65
(dt, 1H), 2.48 (s, 1H), 2.25 (m, 4H), 1.81 (d, 3H, J=1.4 Hz), 1.68 (s,
3H), 1.60 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 146.1, 132.7, 123.4, 120.0,
103.3, 79.0, 33.1, 26.2, 25.7, 23.7, 17.7; HRMS m/z calcd for C11H17Cl3O,
270.0345; found 270.0332. E: 1H NMR (CDCl3, 360 MHz) δ 5.40 (dd, 1H,
J=1.3 Hz, J=8.5 Hz), 5.14 (m, 1H), 4.79 (d, 1H, J=7.9 Hz), 2.59 (s, 1H),
2.15 (m, 4H), 1.83 (d, 3H, J=1.4 Hz), 1.70 (s, 3H), 1.62 (s, 3H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ δ 146.1, 132.7, 123.4, 120.0, 103.3, 79.0, 33.1, 26.2,
25.7, 23.7, 17.7; HRMS m/z calcd for C11H17Cl3O, 270.0345; found
270.0332.
