$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: dl-(E,
E)-3,4-Dihydroxy-1,6-diphenylhexa-1,5-diene (2a): Propionitrile (1.0 mL)
was added to TiI4 (555.5 mg, 1.0 mmol) at ambient temperature under an
argon atmosphere. The solution was stirred for 10 min, and to it was
added a propionitrile (1.0 mL) solution of cinnamaldehyde (66.1 mg, 0.5
mmol) at -78°C. After being stirred at -78°C to -20°C, the reaction was
quenched with sat. aqueous NaHCO3, 10% aqueous NaHSO3, and triethylamine.
The whole mixture was filtered through a Celite pad and extracted with
ethyl acetate (10 mL x 3). The combined organic extracts were dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by preparative
TLC on silica gel (n-hexane : ethyl acetate = 2 : 1 as an eluent) gave
product. dl-(Z,Z)-6,7-Dihydroxy-4,9-diiodododeca-4,8-diene, yield 72%. 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ 0.88 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 6H), 1.47-1.64 (m, 4H), 2.51 (q, J =
7.9 Hz, 4H), 2.60 (s, 2H), 4.34 (d, J = 4.6 Hz, 2H), 5.44 (d, J = 4.6 Hz,
2H). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 12.8, 22.8, 47.5, 78.9, 110.7, 138.7. IR (CHCl3)
3400, 2900, 1650, 1470, 1400, 1130, 1020, 900, 610 cm-1. HRMS calcd for
C12H21O2I2 [M+H]+ 450.97, found 451.68.
