$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Zn(HMDS)2-Catalyzed
Allenylation of Carbonyl Compounds 2a-t with Allenylboronate 1b Zn(HMDS)2
(0.0080 mmol) was dissolved in dry toluene (0.2 mL), and then the
solution was cooled to -40°C or -60°C (depending on the substrates). To
this solution was added dropwise the solution of allenylboronate 1 (0.44
mmol) in dry toluene (0.40 mL), and was then added dropwise a solution of
2 (0.40 mmol) in dry toluene (0.40 mL). When the reaction was conducted
in 8.0 mmol scale, Zn(HMDS)2 and 1b were mixed at 0°C, and after cooled
at -60°C, 2a was added. The mixture was stirred at the same temperature
for 36 h. Then the reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl.
The resultant mixture was allowed to be warmed up to room temperature and
extracted with EtOAc (10 mL*3), and the combined organic layers were
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was evaporated in vacuo, and the
residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography or preparative
thin-layer chromatography. The corresponding allenyl alcohols or mixture
of allenylic/propargyl alcohols. 2-(4-Methoxyphenyl)penta-3,4-dien-2-ol
(3b) 1-(p-Tolyl)buta-2,3-dien-1-ol (3o) 11 1-(p-tolyl)but-3-yn-1-ol (4o)
22 3o: 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz) δ 7.28-7.13 (m, 4H), 5.42-5.41 (m, 1H),
5.22 (s, 1H), 4.91 (m, 2H), 2.34 (s, 3H), 2.23 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
150 MHz) δ 207.0, 139.9, 137.4, 129.1, 126.0, 95.2, 78.0, 71.7, 21.1. 4o:
1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz) δ 7.26 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.16 (d, J = 7.9 Hz,
2H), 4.82 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 2.61 (dd, J = 6.4, 2.6 Hz, 2H), 2.41 (s,
1H), 2.34 (s, 3H), 2.05 (t, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 151 MHz) δ
139.7, 137.8, 129.3, 125.8, 80.9, 72.3, 71.0, 29.4, 21.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, dropwise addition of reactants (stage 1), products depend
on reaction conditions, non-catalyzed reaction gave 6% conversion
