$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the addition of
vinyllithium to aldehydes. The vinyliodide (134 mg, 0.56 mmol.) was
dissolved in diethyl ether (0.3M, 1.9 mL) and the solution was cooled to
-78 °C. Then, t-BuLi (0.68 mL, 1.13 mmol.) was added dropwise and the
mixture stirred for 30 min. at -78 °C and 30 min. at r.t. If
trimethylaluminium was added, it was added at this stage, dropwise and at
25 °C (2.0M in hexanes, 0.70 mL, 1.40 mmol). The mixture was cooled back
down to -78 °C before the aldehyde (69.3 mg, 0.40 mmol) in diethyl ether
was added. The reaction mixture was stirred at -78 °C until the starting
material was consumed (the reaction was monitored by tlc because the time
of reaction vary from a few minutes to a few hours depending on the
presence or absence of AlMe3). Then, the mixture was pourred in a cold (0
°C) sat. aqueous K2CO3 solution until evolution of gas ceased. Then, cold
1N HCl was added to dissolve the white precipitate and the aqueous phase
was extracted with diethyl ether. The combined organic portions were
washed with brine, dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered, and evaporated
under reduced pressure. The ratio of alcohols was determined on the crude
product which was than purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
using hexanes and ethyl acetate as the eluant. (4E)-2-phenyl-4-decen-3-ol
(10 from 9 and 4) See the general procedure above. Obtained as a
colorless oil. Yields: vinyllithium with AlMe3: 73% Major alcohol: 1H
NMR(300MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.34-7.18 (m, 5H), 5.62-5.50 (m, 1H), 5.40-5.30 (m,
1H), 4.19-4.05 (m, 1H), 2.88 (qt, 1H, J=6.5 Hz), 1.96 (q, 2H, J=7 Hz),
1.31 (d, 3H, J= 7 Hz), 1.31-1.10 (m, 6H), 0.86 (t, 3H, J=6.9 Hz). IR
(neat, cm-1): 3557, 3343. LRMS (m/z (relative intensity)): 214 (M+, 20),
143 (100), 127 (80), 105(100). Exact Mass calcd for: C16H24O: 214.1721,
found : 214.1725.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Increased Felkin-Anh Selectivity Using AlMe3 in the Addition of
Vinyllithiums to α-Chiral Aldehydes: Do "Ate" Complexes Play Any Role?
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Spino, Claude; Granger, Marie-Claude; Tremblay, Marie-Claude
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(26), 4735-4737

