$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Alcohol 9 3 To a solution of aldehyde 8 (189 mg, 1.17
mmol) in THF (4 mL) at -78 °C under N2 was added a THF solution of
2-methyl-1-propenylmagnesium bromide (2.80 mL, 0.5 M in THF, 1.40 mmol).
The mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature and was stirred for 4
h. Then the mixture was quenched with water and extracted with ether. The
combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
The resulting residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
(eluting with hexane:ethyl acetate = 9:1) to afford 200 mg (78%) of
alcohol 9 (d.r. 6/5).
